<http://data.silknow.org/object/eb589934-a1ef-3ae8-8896-df0bfdfd72cd/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Thin silks painted with flowers, birds, and butterflies for dress lengths, fan leaves, and screen panels were the final phase of China’s ancient silk trade with the West. The soft ecru ground of this unusual example, suggesting some special kind of unbleached silk, enhances the pearly quality of the white lotus and clematis petals."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/eb589934-a1ef-3ae8-8896-df0bfdfd72cd> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/eb589934-a1ef-3ae8-8896-df0bfdfd72cd>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Thin silks painted with flowers, birds, and butterflies for dress lengths, fan leaves, and screen panels were the final phase of China’s ancient silk trade with the West. The soft ecru ground of this unusual example, suggesting some special kind of unbleached silk, enhances the pearly quality of the white lotus and clematis petals."@en ;
